the fire broke out on Thursday evening  quickly spreading through the unlicensed  orphanage run by a u.s. religious group  just outside Haiti's capital authorities  say seven of those who perished were  babies or toddlers along with six who  were roughly 10 or 11 years of age it  reportedly took firefighters around an  hour and a half to reach the scene we  did not have the means to intervene all  the way off the floor we were taking out  the children who were conscious and  making sure to get them to the hospital  unfortunately when they got to the  hospital they did not receive any help  how the place started is still being  investigated but a worker at the home  said candles were being used for light  after a generator failed the Church of  Bible understanding is reported to have  failed sanitary inspections in the past  because of overcrowding and a lack of  trained staff Pennsylvania organization  which runs this and another home in  Haiti says it houses close to 200  children in what it calls a Christian  training program in Haiti orphans are  often children that families can't  afford to feed they come to places like  this to get an education and safe  housing workers from the home are in  shock I was eating soup and I run fast  to get there when I arrived I did not  find any of my children I saw only three  or four of the younger ones alive the  government has closed around 160  orphanages in the past five years and  hundreds more operate without official  authorization Haiti's president job now  moiez tweeted his condolences saying I'm  deeply saddened by the death of about 10  children as a result of a fire last  night at the orphanage I urged the  authorities to urgently investigate in  order to establish the causes of this  tragedy the authorities say they're  seeking shelter for the children that  survived Ana Gallacher al Jazeera
 

